=== metacharacters stay inside the argument
1=["a&echo INJECTED"]
2=["second"]
1=["a|echo INJECTED"]
2=["second"]
1=["x>made.txt"]
2=["second"]
no file made
=== a quote cannot end the quoting
1=["""&echo INJECTED&"""]
2=["second"]
1=["a\\""&echo INJECTED"]
2=["second"]
1=[""""]
2=["second"]
=== percent signs are not expanded
1=["%OS%"]
2=["100%"]
=== backslashes, empty and spaced arguments
1=["a\\"]
2=["C:\dir\\"]
1=[""]
2=["a b"]
=== ./x.cmd and a PATH lookup both run
1=["one"]
2=[]
1=["two"]
2=[]
=== a line break is refused
wbsh: ./show.bat: an argument with a line break cannot be passed to a batch file
status 126
